	dʒ > j, occasionally ɟ or dʒ in educated speech
	θ ð ðˤ > t d dˤ
	dˤ q > ðˤ ɡ
	a:[+ long] > e:[+ long] / in Form VI (tafā‘ala) verbs, though these apparently coexist with forms having the original vowel as well, with semantic distinctions
	a:[+ long] > æ:[+ long] / when not near emphatics
